{"meta":{"ticker":"SCHD","as_of_date":"2026-09-30","performance_as_of":"2026-09-30","generated_at":"2026-10-01 07:39:59"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"SCHD","fund_name":"Schwab US Dividend Equity ETF","category":"US Large-Cap Value","issuer":"Charles Schwab","index_name":"Dow Jones U.S. Dividend 100","region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.0006,"aum":109559170132,"holdings_count":102,"inception_date":"2011-10-20","overall_score":8.41843659574468,"overall_rank":143,"sector_diversification_score":6.78375826289294},"description":{"tsi_description":"SCHD is a dividend-focused U.S. equity ETF emphasizing profitable U.S. companies with strong dividend sustainability, attractive valuations, and above-average quality characteristics. The strategy prioritizes financially healthy businesses with consistent cash flow generation and shareholder-friendly capital allocation. Many investors find it useful for its uniquely strong combination of dividend yield and dividend growth.","strategy_steps":["The selection process begins with an eligible universe represented by the Schwab U.S. Broad Market ETF (SCHB), excluding REITs.","Securities with float-adjusted market caps below $500 million and three-month average daily value traded less than $2 million are excluded, as are securities that have not paid dividends for at least ten years (i.e., dividend payment years, not dividend growth years).","Next, the Index sorts the remaining securities by their indicated dividend yields and excludes the bottom 50%, narrowing down eligible universe to approximately 375-400.","These remaining securities are ranked based on four fundamental factors (free cash flow divided by total debt, return on equity, indicated dividend yield, and their five-year dividend growth rate), and a composite score is calculated.","The top 100 ranked securities form the Index, though a buffer rule allows current securities to remain in the Index if they rank inside the top 200.","The Index weights securities based on their free-float market caps, with daily reviews ensuring stocks with weights above 4.7% do not exceed 22% cumulatively.","Quarterly rebalancings occur, with a full Index reconstitution implemented after the close of business on the third Friday each March."],"best_for":["Long-term dividend investors","Core equity allocations","Income-focused portfolios"],"strengths":["Strong profitability metrics","Attractive valuation profile","Low expense ratio","High dividend yield and growth"],"watchouts":["Lower exposure to high-growth technology companies","Sector concentration risk","Can lag during speculative growth rallies"],"status":"complete","last_updated":"2026-05-20"},"performance":{"as_of":"2026-09-30","periods":["1M","3M","6M","1Y","3Y","5Y","10Y"],"rows":[{"label":"SCHD","values":{"1M":-6.02568069306929E-02,"3M":3.39574468085106E-02,"6M":7.72300053200923E-02,"1Y":0.245243482469605,"3Y":0.154431182308775,"5Y":9.46721300217224E-02,"10Y":0.12443610094179}},{"label":"SPY","values":{"1M":-3.27201980898484E-03,"3M":2.37987101462438E-02,"6M":0.178605040259332,"1Y":0.157157102167488,"3Y":0.22757633319144,"5Y":0.137031443094805,"10Y":0.15242468944859}},{"label":"+/- SPY","values":{"1M":-5.69847871217081E-02,"3M":1.01587366622669E-02,"6M":-0.10137503493924,"1Y":8.80863803021166E-02,"3Y":-7.31451508826655E-02,"5Y":-4.23593130730824E-02,"10Y":-2.79885885068001E-02}}]},"factor_analysis":{"target":{"costs":9.51329787234043,"liquidity":8.39627659574468,"risk":8.46010638297872,"size":5.84308510638298,"value":7.01595744680851,"dividends":9.87234042553191,"growth":1.13563829787234,"quality":6.75265957446809,"momentum":4.24734042553191,"sentiment":5.93085106382979,"overall":8.41843659574468},"benchmark":{"costs":9.12234042553191,"liquidity":9.83244680851064,"risk":4.31117021276596,"size":2.17287234042553,"value":3.80053191489362,"dividends":8.52393617021277,"growth":7.46276595744681,"quality":8.5